From e41bc0d68ec6c5a32c44db8d95e16a5a7f4d1906 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Cochard <olivier@FreeBSD.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:58:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] snd_acp70: Add a driver for AMD ACP 7.x digital
 microphones
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The built-in microphones of Strix Halo laptops are wired to the ACP's
PDM interface, not to the HDA codec, so FreeBSD had no way to record
from them.  Capture only: no DSP, I2S or SoundWire.

The capture driver, snd_acp_pdm, comes from wulf’s driver for the ACP 6.x
microphones of Lenovo ThinkBooks, so the ACP 6.x PCI drivers can attach
it too.
It now has its own lock: the channel lock recursed in chn_intr() and was
taken on a freed channel by mixer_uninit(), which panicked on kldunload.
It also creates the mixer before pcm_register() and restarts a recording
on resume.

The PCI ID, 1022:15e2, is that of every ACP since Raven, so devmatch(8)
loads snd_acp70 on any Ryzen machine with an ACP; probe keeps revisions
0x70 to 0x72.

Reviewed by:	christos, wulf
Pull Request:	https://ron-dev.freebsd.org/FreeBSD/src/pulls/124
Co-authored-by:	Vladimir Kondratyev <wulf@FreeBSD.org>
