+.Dd November 27, 2026
+.Dt SND_ACP70 4
+.Os
+.Sh NAME
+.Nm snd_acp70
+.Nd "AMD Audio Coprocessor 7.x digital microphone driver"
+.Sh SYNOPSIS
+To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
+kernel configuration file:
+.Bd -ragged -offset indent
+.Cd "device sound"
+.Cd "device snd_acp70"
+.Ed
+.Pp
+Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
+following line in
+.Xr loader.conf 5 :
+.Bd -literal -offset indent
+snd_acp70_load="YES"
+.Ed
+.Pp
+The module loads
+.Pa snd_acp_pdm.ko ,
+the capture driver for the PDM interface, which it depends on.
+.Sh DESCRIPTION
+The
+.Nm
+driver allows the generic audio driver,
+.Xr sound 4 ,
+to record from the built-in digital microphones connected to the PDM
+interface of the AMD Audio Coprocessor (ACP) 7.x.
+It provides one recording channel, stereo, 32-bit signed little-endian
+samples at 48 kHz; the
+.Xr sound 4
+feeders convert to other formats and rates.
+.Pp
+The
+.Xr mixer 8
+input gain
+.Pq Cm igain
+sets the microphones' gain in four steps of about 6 dB; the default, 100,
+is the highest.
+.Pp
+The driver attaches only when the firmware reports digital microphones:
+the ACP pin configuration must route the PDM interface, the ACPI node at
+address 2 below the ACP device must have the
+.Va acp-audio-device-type
+property 2, and the ACPI
+.Va _WOV
+method of the ACP device, when present, must not return 0.
+The ACP's DSP and its I2S and SoundWire links are not used.
+.Sh HARDWARE
+The
+.Nm
+driver supports the following devices:
+.Pp
+.Bl -bullet -compact
+.It
+AMD Audio Coprocessor 7.x (PCI 1022:15e2, revisions 0x70 to 0x72),
+as found in the Ryzen AI Max (Strix Halo) processors
+.El
+.Sh SEE ALSO
+.Xr sound 4 ,
+.Xr mixer 8
+.Sh HISTORY
+The
+.Nm
+driver first appeared in
+.Fx 16.0 .
+.Sh AUTHORS
+.An -nosplit
+The PDM capture driver was written by
+.An Vladimir Kondratyev Aq Mt wulf@FreeBSD.org .
+.An Olivier Cochard Aq Mt olivier@FreeBSD.org
+added the ACP 7.x support.
